  <title>Orca Find</title>
  <p>
    Orca Find searches visible contents in the active window. When there is a match, Orca
    activates flat review and moves the review location to the matching item or text.
  </p>
  <p>
    Finding a match does not move application focus or reposition the caret. To search document
    content beyond the visible portion, use the application's search feature. See "<link xref="features_reading_documents_native_navigation">Native navigation</link>" for application
    search and Orca's presentation of its results.
  </p>
  <section id="commands-find">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Find</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Open the Find dialog</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Keypad Delete</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Left bracket</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Opens a dialog where you can enter text to search for, start from the current location
          or the top of the window, match case, match whole words, search backward, and wrap
          around. Search text is interpreted as a regular expression; characters such as a
          period or an asterisk have special meanings. Use a backslash before a special
          character to match it literally.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Search for the next instance of a string</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Keypad Delete</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Right bracket</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Moves to the next match without reopening the dialog. If you have not searched yet,
          opens the search dialog.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Search for the previous instance of a string</gui>
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              Desktop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Shift</key>
                <key>Keypad Delete</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              Laptop: <keyseq>
                <key>Orca Modifier</key>
                <key>Ctrl</key>
                <key>Right bracket</key>
              </keyseq>
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
        <p>
          Moves to the previous match without reopening the dialog. If you have not searched
          yet, opens the search dialog.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
